.Dd February 28, 2026
.Dt AR 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm ar
.Nd create, modify, and extract archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl
.Ar key
.Op Ar posname
.Ar archive
.Op Ar member ...
.Nm
.Op Fl -format Ns = Ns Ar bsd | gnu
.Op Fl -plugin Ns Oo = Ns Ar path Oc
.Op Fl -verbose
.Ar key
.Op Ar posname
.Ar archive
.Op Ar member ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates and updates archive files.
Archive members are object files or arbitrary byte streams.
.Pp
Operation keys:
.Bl -tag -width "Fl m"
.It Fl r
Replace existing members or add new members.
.It Fl q
Quick append; always appends and does not deduplicate.
.It Fl d
Delete members.
.It Fl t
List members.
.It Fl p
Write member contents to standard output.
.It Fl x
Extract members.
.It Fl m
Move members within the archive.
.It Fl s
Create or update the archive symbol table.
.El
.Pp
Common modifiers:
.Bl -tag -width "Fl -format=gnu"
.It Fl c
Suppress archive creation warning.
.It Fl v
Verbose output.
.It Fl u
Update only when input file is newer than the archived member.
.It Fl a Ar posname
Insert after
.Ar posname
.Pq with Fl r No or Fl m .
.It Fl b Ar posname , Fl i Ar posname
Insert before
.Ar posname
.Pq with Fl r No or Fl m .
.It Fl N Ar count
Operate on the
.Ar count Ns th
instance of duplicate member names
.Pq Fl d , Fl t , Fl x .
.It Fl o
Preserve archived timestamps when extracting.
.It Fl C
Do not overwrite existing files on extraction.
.It Fl U , Fl D
Deterministic mode:
set uid/gid/mtime to 0 and mode to 0644.
.It Fl S
Do not emit symbol tables when writing.
.It Fl T
Create or update as a thin archive.
.It Fl l
Accepted for compatibility (currently a no-op).
.El
.Pp
Long options:
.Bl -tag -width "Fl -format=gnu"
.It Fl -format Ns = Ns Ar bsd | gnu
Select output archive format.
Default is GNU.
.It Fl -plugin Ns Oo = Ns Ar path Oc
Accepted for GCC LTO compatibility; ignored.
.It Fl -verbose
Equivalent to
.Fl v .
.It Fl -no-same-owner
On extraction, do not restore archived uid/gid even when run as root.
.El
.Sh FORMATS
.Nm
supports:
.Bl -bullet
.It
BSD archive format, including
.Dq #1/length
extended names.
.It
GNU/SVR4 archive format, including
.Dq //
long-name tables and
.Dq /offset
name references.
.It
Thin archives
.Pq Dq !<thin>\\n
that store member paths instead of member payloads.
.El
.Pp
GNU symbol tables use
.Dq /
.Pq 32-bit offsets
or
.Dq /SYM64/
.Pq 64-bit offsets
when needed.
BSD symbol tables use
.Dq __.SYMDEF SORTED .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH"
.It Ev ZERO_AR_DATE
If set to a non-empty value, force member mtime to 0 on write.
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
If set to a valid integer epoch value, use it as member mtime on write.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "0"
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Operational failure (I/O, format, allocation, runtime failure).
.It 2
Usage error (invalid options or arguments).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ranlib 1 ,
.Xr ld 1
